WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:07.540
NARRATOR: Out in the deep, the
hunters look even stranger.

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:10.744
[dramatic music]

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:24.124
In the eternal nights of
the abyss, fins and teeth.

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:33.700
A goblin shark.

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:43.943
It has a nose for
prey in the dark

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.912
and knows just how to use it.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:54.621
Most goblin sharks are
10 to 12 feet long,

00:00:54.687 --> 00:01:02.228
but they can grow much bigger,
sluggish until they attack.

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:10.670
[crunching]

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:21.481
These are the fastest
fish jaws in the ocean.

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:26.586
10 feet per second.

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:29.222
So fast they can only
be seen in slow motion.

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:33.460
Only the goblin has
a jaw that whips

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:40.333
forward like a slingshot,
an ancient weapon

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:41.935
that works even today.

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:45.805
[crunching]

